messages.reasoning_content:
The pods in `kube-system` have the label `k8s-app: kube-dns`.

I will update the NetworkPolicy to explicitly allow egress to any pod in the `kube-system` namespace that matches the label `k8s-app: kube-dns` on UDP/53 (and TCP/53 for robustness).

I will use `kubectl patch` on the existing `allow-app-to-dep` policy to add the DNS rule, ensuring I keep the existing dependency rule. This is safer than recreating it.

Existing policy (concept):
```yaml
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: app
  policyTypes:
  - Egress
  egress:
  # Rule 1: Dependency
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          app: dep
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
```

I need to add:
```yaml
  # Rule 2: DNS
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          k8s-app: kube-dns
    ports:
    - protocol: UDP
      port: 53
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 53
```
Since the default patch merges `egress`, I need to provide the full list of egress rules in the JSON patch structure.

I will patch the existing policy to replace the `egress` array with the new, comprehensive list.

The existing policy name is `allow-app-to-dep` in namespace `egress`.

```json
[
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/spec/egress",
    "value": [
      {
        "to": [
          {
            "podSelector": {
              "matchLabels": {
                "app": "dep"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "ports": [
          {
            "protocol": "TCP",
            "port": 80
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "to": [
          {
            "podSelector": {
              "matchLabels": {
                "k8s-app": "kube-dns"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "ports": [
          {
            "protocol": "UDP",
            "port": 53
          },
          {
            "protocol": "TCP",
            "port": 53
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
```
This JSON patch looks correct for replacing the egress list while preserving other metadata.

